    "input": "search_document: I understand you are frustrated and stranded. Based strictly on the provided handbook excerpts, here is the exact outcome of your situation:\n\n**1. You cannot retrieve the item.**\nBecause you missed the 48-hour window to collect the high-value item (priced over $500) from the local depot, the item is officially considered **returned**. The return process has already begun immediately. You are no longer able to pick it up [returns.5].\n\n**2. You will receive a refund, but it is not guaranteed to be \"immediate\" or free of fees.**\n*   **Refund Timing:** The handbook states that refunds are processed within **5 business days** after Northwind receives and inspects the package. The funds then appear in your original payment method within an additional **3 to 7 business days** (or up to 10 days for credit cards) [returns.4]. This aligns with your request for processing within 5 business days of receipt, but please note the additional bank processing time.\n*   **Restocking Fee:** Since the item was not collected and is being returned, it is likely to be inspected. If the item shows any signs of wear, dirt, or damage (which can happen during storage or transit), a **15% restocking fee** will be deducted from your refund [returns.2]. If it is in perfect, unused condition with all tags and packaging intact, no fee is applied [returns.2].\n*   **Shipping Costs:** Standard ground shipping costs for returns are the customer\u2019s responsibility. If you were charged a prepaid label fee of $12.50, that is a flat fee [returns.3]. If you arranged your own shipping, you are responsible for those costs [returns.3].\n\n**3. Important Note on \"Custom\" Items:**\nIf your bike was **custom-configured** or personalized, **no refund will be issued** at all, as these items are non-returnable and non-refundable [returns.6]. If it was a standard model, the refund process described above applies.\n\n**What happens next:**\n1.  The carrier will have already initiated the return to the warehouse because you missed the 48-hour window [returns.5].\n2.  Northwind will receive the package, inspect it, and process the refund within 5 business days of that receipt [returns.4].\n3.  You will receive the funds in your original payment method 3\u201310 business days after the refund is processed [returns.4].\n\n**Escalation:**\nThe handbook excerpts do not provide a mechanism to override the missed 48-hour collection window or to expedite the refund beyond the stated 5-business-day processing window. Since you are requesting an immediate solution that contradicts the strict policy timelines and the automatic return status, I must escalate this ticket to a human agent to see if any exceptions can be made for your specific circumstances.\n\n[returns.5]\n[returns.4]\n[returns.2]\n[returns.6]",
